-- credits: https://github.com/create-dmg/create-dmg
-- Override of the javapackager DMG customization template.
--
-- On headless/CI environments (e.g. CircleCI macOS VMs) Finder often cannot service
-- container-window manipulation AppleEvents: they hang until the AppleEvent timeout
-- expires and raise -1712, which makes javapackager fail the DMG step (it then
-- produces no DMG at all). Simple events (like `get name`) do work.
--
-- This variant therefore:
--   * wraps the whole customization in `with timeout of 60 seconds`, and
--   * on ANY error (including a -1712 timeout), logs the failure and bails out
--     cleanly so the DMG is still produced (plain, without background image / icon
--     layout) instead of aborting the whole DMG generation.
-- The timeout is kept short (60s) on purpose: a hanging Finder must fail fast so the
-- enclosing Maven build step (10 min limit on CircleCI) cannot time out.
--
-- Error handling structure (important):
--   The `try` wraps the ENTIRE `tell application "Finder"` block. A -1712 timeout is
--   "sticky": even when caught, the pending reply poisons the still-active `tell`
--   scope, so the tell-block teardown (or any further command in that scope, such as
--   the error handler's own `log`) re-raises -1712 and kills osascript anyway. By
--   catching OUTSIDE the tell blocks the error unwinds the whole tell stack (nothing
--   is left to re-raise), and the handler runs in a scope with no Finder connection.
--   The handler must not itself issue any AppleEvent to Finder; the final `log` is
--   also placed at top level, outside any `tell` context.
-- The .DS_STORE wait loop is bounded so a Finder that never writes the file cannot
-- hang the build either.
on run (volumeName)
	set finalMessage to ""
	try
		tell application "Finder"
			tell disk (volumeName as string)
				open

				with timeout of 60 seconds
					set theXOrigin to ${info.macConfig.windowX}
					set theYOrigin to ${info.macConfig.windowY}
					set theWidth to ${info.macConfig.windowWidth}
					set theHeight to ${info.macConfig.windowHeight}

					set theBottomRightX to (theXOrigin + theWidth)
					set theBottomRightY to (theYOrigin + theHeight)
					set dsStore to "\"/Volumes/" & volumeName & "/.DS_STORE\""

					tell container window
						set current view to icon view
						set toolbar visible to false
						set statusbar visible to false
						set the bounds to {theXOrigin, theYOrigin, theBottomRightX, theBottomRightY}
						set position of every item to {theBottomRightX + 100, 100}
					end tell

					set opts to the icon view options of container window
					tell opts
						set icon size to ${info.macConfig.iconSize}
						set text size to ${info.macConfig.textSize}
						set arrangement to not arranged
					end tell
					set background picture of opts to file ".background:background.png"

					-- Positioning
					set position of item "${info.appFile.name}" to {${info.macConfig.iconX}, ${info.macConfig.iconY}}

					-- Hiding
					set the extension hidden of item "${info.appFile.name}" to true

					-- Application
					set position of item "Applications" to {${info.macConfig.appsLinkIconX}, ${info.macConfig.appsLinkIconY}}

					close
					open
					-- Force saving of the size
					delay 1

					tell container window
						set statusbar visible to false
						set the bounds to {theXOrigin, theYOrigin, theBottomRightX - 10, theBottomRightY - 10}
					end tell

					delay 1

					tell container window
						set statusbar visible to false
						set the bounds to {theXOrigin, theYOrigin, theBottomRightX, theBottomRightY}
					end tell

					--give the finder some time to write the .DS_Store file
					delay 3

					set waitTime to 0
					set ejectMe to false
					repeat while ejectMe is false and waitTime < 120
						delay 1
						set waitTime to waitTime + 1
						if (do shell script "[ -f " & dsStore & " ]; echo $?") = "0" then set ejectMe to true
					end repeat
					if waitTime = 120 then set finalMessage to "Timed out waiting for .DS_STORE; continuing anyway."
					if finalMessage = "" then set finalMessage to "waited " & waitTime & " seconds for .DS_STORE to be created."
				end timeout
			end tell
		end tell
		set finalMessage to "customization done"
	on error errMsg number errNum
		set finalMessage to "DMG customization skipped: Finder error " & errNum & ": " & errMsg
	end try
	log finalMessage
end run
